      "id": 1,
      "text": "Kit Carson was founded in 1838 and named after frontiersman Christopher Houston 'Kit' Carson.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kit_Carson%2C_Colorado",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "By the 1870s, Kit Carson had become one of the largest cattle shipping points between Denver and Kansas City.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        19
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kit_Carson%2C_Colorado",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The arrival of the Union Pacific railroad in 1870 turned Kit Carson into the railroad terminus, sparking rapid growth.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5,
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.townofkitcarson.com/about",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "In 1872, a permanent garrison of 100 regular army men was stationed in Kit Carson to protect the frontier.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        17
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.townofkitcarson.com/about",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Kit Carson’s original site sits near where the scout traded with Arapahoe and Cheyenne Indians, linking it to early Native trade.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        28
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.townofkitcarson.com/about",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "The town survived three fires—twice by Indian torches and once by cowboys—rebuilding each time to show resilience.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        29
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
